<h1 id=3D"PlatformAccessManagement(PAM)-PlatformAccessManagementPrinciples"=
>Platform Access Management Principles</h1>
<ul>
 <li><span>PAM focuses on consumer-facing access enablement </span>rather t=
han operational work management<span>;</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"21aefc3c-16a4-4a6b-ad39-5bdd5b25a488">PAM shall avoid bui=
lding generic service management capabilities;</li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"d78bbbeb-d4fa-49eb-83c0-28a42bc8f1dc"><span>PAM shall rem=
ain compatible with future workflow platform integration;</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"162417c8-3c23-49f0-bf44-b850e6093918"><span>Status is der=
ived from business events;</span></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"591616ce-f894-4149-a960-fe18def38e30"><span>Operational a=
ctions are owned by producer systems.</span></li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"PlatformAccessManagement(PAM)-ArchitecturalContext">Architectural=
 Context</h1>
<p class=3D"___1sql8mq f1rh9g5y f11qrl6u f19n0e5 fibxuh5 f4fkekg">The follo=
wing statements provide context for understanding the scope, responsibiliti=
es, and interactions of Platform Access Management (PAM):</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"35623f22-cfaa-4a39-a713-a9a9ad7a5cdf">
  <p>PAM is not the system of record for identity, entitlement, or access e=
nforcement;</p>
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"7ab844f5-6357-4a42-a2a1-a6c3dd9e259b">
    <p class=3D"___1sql8mq f1rh9g5y f11qrl6u f19n0e5 fibxuh5 f4fkekg">Firm =
and User Management (FUM) remains the system of record for identity, entitl=
ement, and access governance capabilities.</p></li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"98cb88e0-e4f3-4dcb-bc4b-659a52c0283b">
  <p>PAM provides consumer-facing access request capabilities;</p>
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"3a32a4ab-91ce-4366-95e6-e8267bbf6d20">
    <p class=3D"___1sql8mq f1rh9g5y f11qrl6u f19n0e5 fibxuh5 f4fkekg">PAM e=
nables consumers to discover available services and features, submit access=
 requests, track request status, and receive request-related notifications.=
</p></li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"183b4e9a-fb85-434f-9573-a385ea269bad">
  <p>Producer systems may emit request lifecycle events;</p>
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"646bec7c-b155-40af-bf01-2ea73dd4f31b">
    <p class=3D"___1sql8mq f1rh9g5y f11qrl6u f19n0e5 fibxuh5 f4fkekg">Produ=
cers may include FUM, administrative interfaces, or other authorized system=
s.</p></li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"3474cfd4-1e48-4f54-b2c9-b8f07b2be339">
  <p>FUM and other producer systems may generate lifecycle events that infl=
uence request status;</p>
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"c0f4b44e-9698-4e8b-ab4a-ab19024eb3eb">
    <p class=3D"___1sql8mq f1rh9g5y f11qrl6u f19n0e5 fibxuh5 f4fkekg">PAM d=
erives request status from recorded lifecycle events.</p></li>
  </ul></li>
 <li data-uuid=3D"8be59c44-1eeb-4fe9-a28f-1c719d8ec8eb">
  <p class=3D"___1sql8mq f1rh9g5y f11qrl6u f19n0e5 fibxuh5 f4fkekg">Request=
 status provides consumer-facing visibility into the progression of an acce=
ss request;</p>
  <ul>
   <li data-uuid=3D"35ba1f0b-eec1-4e8d-9e4b-3496edb3242d">
    <p class=3D"___1sql8mq f1rh9g5y f11qrl6u f19n0e5 fibxuh5 f4fkekg">Reque=
st status does not represent operational work tracking, task management, wo=
rkflow state, queue state, or service management activities.</p></li>
  </ul></li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"PlatformAccessManagement(PAM)-ArchitectureOverview">Architecture =
Overview</h1>
